    cuisine="Full English Breakfast (the hearty classic: fried eggs, crispy back bacon rashers, Cumberland pork sausages, baked Heinz beans, grilled tomatoes, sautéed field mushrooms, black pudding, and buttered toast with hot tea), Sunday Roast (roasted sirloin of beef, lamb, or chicken served with crispy roast potatoes, roasted parsnips, steamed vegetables, giant puffed golden Yorkshire puddings, and drenched in rich beef bone gravy, accompanied by fiery English horseradish), Fish and Chips (fresh Atlantic cod or haddock fillets coated in crisp golden beer batter, served with thick-cut chips, mushy peas, and tartar sauce, sprinkled with malt vinegar and sea salt), Shepherd's Pie and Cottage Pie (minced lamb or beef simmered with onions, carrots, and peas in rich gravy, topped with creamy piped mashed potatoes and baked golden brown), Beef Wellington (tender beef tenderloin fillet coated with mushroom duxelles, wrapped in prosciutto and golden puff pastry), Chicken Tikka Masala (invented in Britain by South Asian chefs, universally hailed as a true British national dish), Cornish Pasty (crimp-sealed pastry filled with diced beef skirt, potato, swede, and onion - PGI), Afternoon Tea (warm freshly baked scones served with strawberry jam and thick Devonshire or Cornish clotted cream / cream tea, finger sandwiches, and tea), British Cheeses (Cheddar, blue Stilton, Red Leicester), and Desserts: Sticky Toffee Pudding (warm moist date sponge cake smothered in rich buttery toffee sauce and vanilla custard), Eton Mess, Apple Crumble, and Scotch Whisky (Single Malt Scotch from Speyside, Islay, Highlands).",
    festivals=["Glastonbury Festival (world's premier contemporary performing arts and music festival held at Worthy Farm in Somerset)", "Edinburgh Festival Fringe (world's largest arts festival, transforming Scotland's capital with thousands of theatrical performances every August)", "Notting Hill Carnival in London (Europe's largest vibrant Caribbean street carnival held on August Bank Holiday)", "Trooping the Colour (His Majesty's Birthday Parade in London with the Royal Family on the Buckingham Palace balcony)", "Wimbledon Tennis Championships", "The Proms (classical concerts at Royal Albert Hall concluding with the patriotic 'Last Night of the Proms')", "Guy Fawkes Night / Bonfire Night (November 5 - bonfires and fireworks commemorating the 1605 Gunpowder Plot)"],
