    sports="The cradle of modern sports (the UK invented or codified: Association Football, Cricket, Rugby Union, Rugby League, Tennis, Golf, and Field Hockey): Football (Premier League - the most watched and lucrative sports league on Earth; 1966 FIFA World Cup Champions; Harry Kane, Jude Bellingham, David Beckham, Bobby Charlton), Cricket (invented in England; 2019 Cricket World Cup Champions; The Ashes against Australia), Tennis (Wimbledon Championships at the All England Club - oldest and most prestigious tennis tournament on Earth, played on grass; Sir Andy Murray - double Olympic Gold and double Wimbledon Champion), Formula 1 (Sir Lewis Hamilton - record 7-time World Champion and 105+ Grand Prix wins), Golf (invented in Scotland: St Andrews Old Course - 'The Home of Golf'; The Open Championship), Athletics (Sir Mo Farah - quadruple Olympic Gold distance champion; Sir Roger Bannister - first sub-4-minute mile).",
