    flagDescription="The Union Flag, popularly known as the Union Jack: combines the red cross of Saint George (patron saint of England, edged with white) with the white diagonal saltire of Saint Andrew (patron saint of Scotland) on a deep navy-blue field, combined with the red diagonal saltire of Saint Patrick (patron saint of Ireland), edged with white.",
    coatOfArmsDescription="Quartered shield: first and fourth quarters gules with three golden lions passant guardant (England); second quarter or with a red lion rampant within a double tressure flory-counterflory (Scotland); third quarter azure with a golden harp stringed argent (Ireland); surrounded by the Garter with the motto 'Honi soit qui mal y pense' (Shame on him who thinks evil of it); supported by the crowned English Lion on the dexter and the chained Scottish Unicorn on the sinister, resting upon a floral terrace bearing the national motto 'DIEU ET MON DROIT' (God and my right).",
    symbols={"crest": "The Royal Arms / Union Jack", "floralEmblems": "Tudor Rose (England), Thistle (Scotland), Leek and Daffodil (Wales), Shamrock and Flax (Northern Ireland)", "animal": "Lion / Unicorn / Red deer", "bird": "European robin (Robin redbreast)"},
    landmarks=["Palace of Westminster and Elizabeth Tower / Big Ben (London)", "Tower of London and Tower Bridge", "Stonehenge Megalithic Monument (Wiltshire)", "Edinburgh Castle and the Royal Mile (Scotland)", "Giant's Causeway (Northern Ireland)", "Buckingham Palace (London)", "Windsor Castle (world's oldest and largest occupied castle)", "St. Paul's Cathedral (London)", "Roman Baths and Royal Crescent (Bath)", "Loch Ness and Urquhart Castle (Scottish Highlands)", "Canterbury Cathedral"],
    travelNotes="Listen to the resonant chimes of Big Ben echoing across the River Thames from Westminster Bridge; stand before the mysterious 4,500-year-old stone circles of Stonehenge at dawn; walk the cobbled Royal Mile from the Palace of Holyroodhouse up to Edinburgh Castle perched on an extinct volcano; explore the Roman Baths in golden Georgian Bath; savor a Sunday roast with Yorkshire pudding and a pint of hand-pulled cask ale in a cozy village pub.",
