    travelNotes="Stand in the center of Bernini's sweeping elliptical colonnades in Saint Peter's Square gazing up at the great dome; step inside Saint Peter's Basilica to marvel at Michelangelo's heartbreakingly beautiful Pietà carved from a single block of Carrara marble; gaze in silent wonder at the ceiling of the Sistine Chapel as Adam's finger reaches toward God; climb the 551 steps to the top of Michelangelo's dome for an unforgettable 360-degree panorama of Rome; send a postcard from the Vatican Post Office with a genuine Vatican stamp.",
